.TH "OPS" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops \- run the fleet
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops\fR [flags] <command>
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBnote\fR
add a note
.TP
\fBexec\fR
run a command
.SH "DATA"
Commands that read a document from standard input.
.TP
\fBimport\fR
import tasks
.TP
\fBupper\fR
upper\-case lines
.SH "DEPLOYING"
Commands that change what runs where.
Each one asks before it acts.
.TP
\fBdeploy\fR
ship a service
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.SH "OUTPUT"
Flags that shape what ops prints.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more (repeatable)
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBOPS_TOKEN\fR \fIstring\fR
the API token (length >= 20)
.br
at least 20 characters
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
\fBregion\fR (region) \fIstring\fR
the default region
.br
must look like eu\-1
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\-deploy\fR(1), \fBops\-import\fR(1), \fBops\-upper\fR(1),
\fBops\-note\fR(1), \fBops\-exec\fR(1)
